/-!
# VIII09 — the real ε³ source dictionary

The task-book sources are

  `S3 = (u-2z) b1/R - P z' b1' + 2Q u (j + 2Q b1)/R³`,  `q3_j(1/R) = R³ S3`,
  `r3_j(1/R) = R⁴ (u+z) v1'`,

built from the **actual** first-order and second-order anchor data
`b1 = bstar 3 1 (3/2) j`, `v1 = vstar 3 1 j`, `u = uA j`, `z = zA j`, `P = N/R`, `Q = 3/2`.

Here the transported profiles `Utilde = j² x Ū(x)`, `Ztilde = j² x Z̄(x)` at `x = 1/R` are proved
equal to the anchor data (`uA_transport`, `zA_transport`), and the sources built from them are
proved equal to the **compact** closed profiles `q3_j`, `r3_j` of `Compact.lean`.  So the compact
source is not a substitution: it is the same object.
-/

set_option maxHeartbeats 1600000

open Set Filter Topology MeasureTheory intervalIntegral
